      "message": "Assuming we don\u0027t just consolidate to one block that always supports swizzles, this seems like it will lead to more pipeline compilations around non-yuv image shaders and we lose the identity colorspace xform short-circuiting for the image shaders when the swizzle is RGBA or BGRA.\n\nWhat if we had two different `AddBlocks`, one for the non-image case that always does the no-swizzle version w/ no short-circuit, and one for the image+swizzle case (and probably have YUV images use that one to get the short circuiting)?",
